                        "username": "kokilavaradhan"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net @abhilash.kollam@gmail.com\nAbhilash's concern is valid. Re-accepting on all ports after a single port receives a connection is inefficient. Each acceptor should independently manage its own accept cycle. The current fix properly addresses the socket reuse bug without introducing unnecessary overhead."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_server.hpp",
                    "line": 152,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "That's not what the \"critical bug\" reported was.  Sure, if we want to reuse, we can, and that's fine.  I don't really want to argue here."
                }
